{%- comment -%}
  DIAMOND SHAPE OUTLINES.

  Drawn here as inline SVG rather than uploaded as images, for three reasons:

  1. There are no diamond-shape assets in this theme — the existing icon
     snippets are UI chrome (accordion carets, social marks). Something had
     to be made.
  2. A photograph of a diamond is inventory. These are category outlines, so
     drawing them avoids putting a picture of a stone we do not have in
     front of a customer.
  3. They inherit `currentColor` and scale, so one file serves the shape grid
     and anywhere else a shape needs naming later.

  The outlines are the stone's TABLE VIEW — the silhouette seen from above,
  which is how every diamond search in the trade draws them. Deliberately
  plain silhouettes with no facet lines: at 40px the facets turn to mud, and
  a wrong facet pattern on an Asscher would be a claim about the cut.

  THE ATTRIBUTES ARE CAPTURED, THE TAG IS NOT. The first version of this file
  captured `<svg ...>` as an opening fragment and reused it in every branch,
  which theme-check rejected outright:

      LiquidHTMLSyntaxError — Attempting to close LiquidTag 'capture'
      before it was opened

  Liquid's HTML parser balances tags across capture boundaries, so half a tag
  in a variable is not a thing that can exist. Capturing only the attribute
  list keeps every tag closed where it is opened, at the cost of repeating
  eleven characters per branch.

  Usage:
    {% render 'carat-diamond-shape-icon', shape: 'round', size: 40 %}

  An unknown shape renders nothing rather than a fallback blob, so a typo is
  visible as an absence instead of silently drawing the wrong stone.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign s = shape | default: '' | downcase
  assign px = size | default: 40
-%}

{%- capture a -%}
class="cd-shape__icon" width="{{ px }}" height="{{ px }}" viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- case s -%}
  {%- when 'round' -%}
    <svg {{ a }}><circle cx="24" cy="24" r="18" /></svg>

  {%- when 'oval' -%}
    <svg {{ a }}><ellipse cx="24" cy="24" rx="12.5" ry="18" /></svg>

  {%- comment -%}
    EMERALD / RADIANT / ASSCHER ARE SEPARATED BY PROPORTION, NOT BY DETAIL.

    All three are cut-corner silhouettes, and the first version of this file
    drew them at near-identical sizes — on the rendered page they were three
    indistinguishable octagons, which makes a shape picker worse than no
    shape picker. The trade separates them by aspect ratio, so these do too:

      emerald  22 x 40  clearly elongated
      radiant  30 x 34  rectangular but broad
      asscher  34 x 34  square, with corner cuts deep enough to read

    Checked at 44px, the size the shape grid actually renders.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- when 'emerald' -%}
    <svg {{ a }}><path d="M19 4h10l6 6v28l-6 6H19l-6-6V10z" /></svg>

  {%- when 'radiant' -%}
    <svg {{ a }}><path d="M15 7h18l6 6v22l-6 6H15l-6-6V13z" /></svg>

  {%- when 'cushion' -%}
    <svg {{ a }}><rect x="7" y="7" width="34" height="34" rx="11" /></svg>

  {%- when 'princess' -%}
    <svg {{ a }}><rect x="8" y="8" width="32" height="32" /></svg>

  {%- when 'asscher' -%}
    <svg {{ a }}><path d="M17 7h14l10 10v14l-10 10H17L7 31V17z" /></svg>

  {%- when 'pear' -%}
    <svg {{ a }}><path d="M24 4c8 9 14 18 14 25a14 14 0 0 1-28 0C10 22 16 13 24 4z" /></svg>

  {%- when 'marquise' -%}
    <svg {{ a }}><path d="M24 4c7 8 11 15 11 20s-4 12-11 20c-7-8-11-15-11-20s4-12 11-20z" /></svg>

  {%- when 'heart' -%}
    <svg {{ a }}><path d="M24 42C9 31 5 22 5 16.5A10.5 10.5 0 0 1 24 11a10.5 10.5 0 0 1 19 5.5C43 22 39 31 24 42z" /></svg>
{%- endcase -%}
